<title>UK: Brixton buys estates for 8.0 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Brixton buys estates for 8.0 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Property firm Brixton Estate Plc said on Friday that it has bought two industrial/warehouse investments in southern England for 8.0 million stg in cash.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement it acquired an industrial estate in Crawley from Associated British Foods Pension Trustees Ltd and a distribution centre from Royal London Mutual Insurance Society.</p>
<p>Brixton said that the acquisitions were part of its strategy of reinvesting in industrial and warehouse estates in the south east of Britain.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom - +44 171 542 4019</p>
